__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
.venv*/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# Written by `assurance pin --save`; never this repo's own, and tests must not create it.
.assurance/
.mypy_cache/

# Written by uv when it resolves an environment, which any `uv run` does in whichever package
# directory it is invoked from, with or without `--with`. A plain `pytest` run through an existing
# virtualenv does not, which is the half both people who have debugged this got wrong, so it is
# worth stating: this rule is insurance, not a response to something recurring.
# This repository tracks no lockfile of any kind, so one arriving here would be a dependency
# decision nobody made, and one did arrive that way on a feature branch, swept into an unrelated
# commit by a broad `git add`. An ignore rule does not untrack anything, and nothing here is.
uv.lock
